  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Agroecology for Sustainable Food Systems in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Strengthening Agroecology for Sustainable Food Systems in Africa&quot; project is a collaborative effort between CAFOD and AFSA. It aims to address the challenges within the African food system by promoting agroecology and supporting smallholder food producers, particularly in the face of increasing concentration of power, exclusion, injustice, and a consolidated push for industrial farming in policies and investments. The project seeks to strengthen communities, empower farmers, advocate for policies that benefit smallholder food producers, and transition towards sustainable food systems. It will enhance collaboration between CAFOD and AFSA and promote coordinated advocacy efforts across countries, regions, and at the global level.</narrative>
  </description>
